"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with a kick-off on June 15th. The initial budget was $500,000, but it was later adjusted to $550,000 to cover unforeseen expenses and real-time analytics integration. The project involves gathering AI-driven ideas for data visualization by July 20th and expanding the team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, who joined in an onboarding session on September 10th. A significant milestone was reached with the successful completion of the testing phase and prototype testing for secure file sharing ahead of schedule. The project also includes a compliance plan with a budget of $55,000 for training and audits, as well as a separate $15,000 approved budget for specialized coding and project manager training. A celebration for the milestone is scheduled for October 10th, with the next phase focusing on user interface enhancements commencing in October."
